REOPENING consideration -- my close was too strong. I verified the pairing but not fixTurnFinished itself:

  const fixTurnFinished = (event) => {
    const results = event?.toolResults;
    return Array.isArray(results) && results.length === 0;
  };

That is 'the turn ended with no tool calls', i.e. the model gave a final answer. So the window closes at the first tool-free turn -- NOT at every turn_end, which is what I implied when closing this.

Consequence: while the model keeps calling tools, the window stays open across turns. In an interactive session the user's own interleaved messages can fall inside that span, which is this bead's original complaint ('grants applied to unrelated user-directed work for several replies'). It is narrower than before -- it ends at the first tool-free turn rather than at agent_end -- but it is not eliminated.

Status: PARTIALLY fixed. The agent_end/turn_end closes are real improvements; the residual is that a long tool-using stretch keeps the window open over work that is not the fix turn's.
